  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of rounded pastel figures with hooded heads descending stairs beside a mint green subway train, signed CRUMP 11.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on wood, signed CRUMP 11 at lower left. A mint green subway train with white windows and doors runs along the top and recedes to the right. Below, a crowd of rounded figures in lilac, pink, yellow, mint and green, each with a hooded head topped by a tan or green cap and mitten hands, walks down a platform and a flight of white stairs toward the lower right. One figure at lower right holds a white square like a phone, and one at left looks down with a round pink patch. Thick black outlines over flat pastel colour with visible brushwork.",
    "impression": "A New York commute translated into the soft creatures of the town series: the puffer jacket crowd going underground. The hoods and caps make everybody anonymous in the way subway crowds are. It is affectionate and specific, a real place made gentle.",
